Subject: [PATCH] net/tcp: allow congestion avoidance to recover after timeouts

NewReno's max_cwnd is initialized from the peer window and reduced on every
RTO, but never increased afterwards. Congestion avoidance cannot grow beyond
that historical ceiling even after arbitrarily many successful ACKs. A few
early timeouts can therefore leave a long-lived connection permanently slow.

Remove the extra ceiling and its private field. Retain the existing RTO
reduction to one SMSS, ssthresh calculation, additive increase and saturating
arithmetic. The buffered send gate already limits flight to the smaller of
the current peer window and cwnd. This follows RFC 5681 section 3.1 without
adding a buffer, tuning parameter or application-specific exception.

--- a/net/tcp/tcp.h
+++ b/net/tcp/tcp.h
@@ -249,7 +249,6 @@
 
   uint32_t cwnd;          /* The Congestion window */
-  uint32_t max_cwnd;      /* The Congestion window maximum value */
   uint32_t ssthresh;      /* The Slow start threshold */
 #endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_NET_TCP_WINDOW_SCALE
   uint32_t snd_wnd;       /* Sequence and acknowledgement numbers of last
--- a/net/tcp/tcp_cc.c
+++ b/net/tcp/tcp_cc.c
@@ -163,7 +163,6 @@
     {
       conn->last_ackno = tcp_getsequence(tcp->ackno);
       CC_INIT_CWND(conn->cwnd, conn->mss);
-      conn->max_cwnd = conn->snd_wnd;
       conn->ssthresh = MAX(conn->snd_wnd, conn->ssthresh);
     }
 }
@@ -294,7 +293,6 @@
               increase = MAX((conn->mss * conn->mss / conn->cwnd), 1);
 
               CC_CWND_INC(conn->cwnd, increase);
-              conn->cwnd = MIN(conn->cwnd, conn->max_cwnd);
               ninfo("update congestion avoidance cwnd to %u\n", conn->cwnd);
             }
         }
--- a/net/tcp/tcp_timer.c
+++ b/net/tcp/tcp_timer.c
@@ -634,10 +634,6 @@
                         conn->flags &= ~TCP_INFR;
                       }
 
-                    /* update the max_cwnd */
-
-                    conn->max_cwnd = (conn->max_cwnd + 7 * conn->cwnd) >> 3;
-
                     /* reset cwnd and ssthresh, refers to RFC5861. */
 
                     conn->ssthresh =
--- a/Documentation/reference/os/newreno.rst
+++ b/Documentation/reference/os/newreno.rst
@@ -8,7 +8,11 @@
  - Fast Retransmission
  - Fast Recovery.
 
- The implementation refers to RFC6582 and RFC5681. In addition, we optimize the congestion algorithm. In the congestion avoidance state, the maximum congestion window (max_cwnd) is used to limit the excessive growth of cwnd and prevent network jitter caused by congestion. Maximum congestion window (max_cwnd) is updated with the current congestion window (cwnd) and the update weight is 0.875 when an RTO timeout occurs.
+The implementation refers to RFC6582 and RFC5681. Congestion avoidance grows
+the congestion window after successful acknowledgments. A timeout reduces
+the window and restarts slow start; it does not impose a permanent historical
+ceiling on later growth. The peer's advertised window still limits how many
+bytes may be sent.
 
 Workflow
 ========
@@ -25,9 +29,9 @@
 
    * If the current ackno is bigger than fr_ack which is the snd_seq when Fast Retransmission occurs, exit the Fast Recovery state and enter to congestion avoidance.
    * If the cwnd is less than ssthresh, increase the cwnd on slow start state.
-   * If the cwnd is greater than or equal to ssthresh, the increased cwnd can not exceed max_cwnd.
+   * If the cwnd is greater than or equal to ssthresh, grow cwnd additively in congestion avoidance.
 
-- when RTO times out, reset the values of cwnd and ssthresh, update the max_cwnd, and enter to Slow Start state.
+- When RTO times out, reset cwnd to one SMSS, update ssthresh, and enter the Slow Start state.
 - When sending a segment, the minimum value of cwnd and snd_wnd is used to calculate the number of bytes that can be sent.
 
 The simple state transition diagram of the NewReno is shown below.
@@ -45,7 +49,7 @@
              |    timeout          |  |  recv dup ack        | recv new ack
              |------------------   |  |  ---------------     | ----------------
              |reset cwnd ssthresh  |  |  dupack >= 3         | cwnd >= ssthresh
-             |update max_cwnd      |  |  fr_ack = snd_seq    |
+             |                    |  |  fr_ack = snd_seq    |
              |<--------------------'  |<------------------.  |
              |                        |                   |  |
              |                        v                   |  V
